1. d4 Nf6 2. Bg5 e6 3. e4 h6 4. Bxf6 Qxf6 5. Nf3 d6 6. Nc3 Nd7 7. Qd2 a6 8. a4
g6 9. h4 Bg7 10. Be2 Qe7 11. a5 c6 {[ 11..h5 and 12..0-0 was better, Black
creates weaknesses on b6 and allows his bishop to become bad after h5 g5 and
these problems eventually lead to the loss of the game. ]} 12. Na4 e5 13. dxe5
dxe5 14. h5 $16 g5 15. Qc3 O-O 16. Nd2 Rb8 17. Bg4 Rd8 18. f3 Nf8 19. Bxc8
Rbxc8 20. O-O-O Ne6 21. Nb6 Rb8 22. g4 Nd4 23. Qc4 Bf8 24. Rhe1 Qf6 25. c3 Ne6
26. Qf1 Bc5 27. Ndc4 Bxb6 28. axb6 {[ Now the weakness of the b7 pawn would be
decisive in an endgame so White exchanges pieces ]} Nf8 29. Rxd8 Rxd8 30. Rd1
Qe7 31. Rxd8 Qxd8 32. Kc2 Qe7 33. Qd3 Nd7 34. Qd6 $18 {[#]} Qxd6 35. Nxd6 Nxb6
36. Nxb7 f6 37. Kb3 Kf8 38. Nd6 a5 39. Nf5 c5 40. c4 a4+ 41. Kc3 Na8 42. Nxh6
Nc7 43. Nf5 Ne6 44. Nd6 Nd4 45. Nb7 Nxf3 46. Nxc5 Nh2 47. Ne6+ Kf7 48. h6 Kg6
49. c5 Nxg4 50. c6 Nf2 51. Nc5 1-0

