1. e4 c5 2. c3 e6 3. d4 d5 4. e5 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bd7 6. Be2 Nge7 7. Na3 Ng6 8. Nc2
Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. Be3 Kh8 11. Nd2 $6 Qb6 12. Rb1 f6 13. f4 Nh4 $1 $15 14. Nf3
Nxf3+ 15. Rxf3 fxe5 16. fxe5 Rxf3 17. Bxf3 Be8 {[ /\ Bg6 -/+ ]} 18. Bh5 cxd4
19. cxd4 Bxh5 20. Qxh5 Qa6 $1 $17 21. Rf1 $1 {[ The best practical chance,
White sacrifices two pawns and comes close to saving the game. 21.a3 Qd3 was
unpleasant ]} Qxa2 22. Qf7 Qxb2 23. Bg5 Qxc2 (23... Bxg5 $4 24. Qf8+ $18) 24.
Bxe7 Nxe7 25. Qxe7 Qc8 26. Rf7 {[#] [ The high point of White's counterplay,
but Black has an excellent riposte going passive with 26..Qg8 allows lines
like 27.Qxb7 a5 28.Rxg7! ]} Qc1+ $1 27. Kf2 Qc2+ 28. Kg3 (28. Ke1 Qe4+ 29. Kf2
h6 30. Rxg7 Rc8 $19) 28... Qg6+ {[ The rest is very easy ]} 29. Kh3 Qh6+ 30.
Kg4 Rg8 31. g3 a5 32. h4 Qg6+ 33. Kh3 b5 34. g4 h6 35. h5 Qd3+ 36. Kg2 Qe4+ 37.
Kg3 Rc8 38. Rf3 Rc1 39. Qxe6 Qe1+ 40. Kh3 Qh1+ 41. Kg3 Rg1+ 42. Kf4 Qh2+ 0-1

