1. d4 d6 2. e4 g6 3. Nc3 c6 4. Be3 Bg7 5. Qd2 b5 6. f3 Nd7 {[ Black plays the
modern move order delaying ..Nf6 to prevent Bh6 etc. Mestel was hoping to lure
Black into an unsound attack and he succeeds ]} 7. g4 $5 {[ A common enough
move but h4 first is a better bet. Black realises White might be intending h4
and that is a positional error since it can be met by ..h5 so cunningly Black
does nothing to deflect White from his plan ]} Rb8 8. h4 $6 h5 $1 9. g5 e6 10.
f4 b4 11. Nce2 Ne7 12. Ng3 {[ Now White goes for f5 ]} c5 13. Nf3 Bb7 14. Bd3
O-O {[ White is totally becalmed and his king has nowhere safe to go. The pin
on the b7 h1 diagonal prevents f5 and Black's queen side play is taking over ]}
15. c3 bxc3 16. bxc3 cxd4 17. cxd4 Nc5 $1 18. O-O {[ Now White is cut up by
two bishops but 18.Bc2 Ba6 was not palatable either ]} Nxd3 19. Qxd3 Qa5 20.
Bd2 Qa4 21. Rfc1 Ba6 22. Qe3 Rfc8 23. Bc3 Rc7 24. Ne2 Rbc8 25. Bb2 Rc2 26. Nc3
R8xc3 $1 {[#]} 27. Bxc3 Re2 28. Bd2 Rxe3 29. Bxe3 Be2 0-1

