1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bb5 g6 5. h3 {[ /\ e5 ]} Qc7 6. O-O Bg7 7.
Re1 a6 8. e5 $1 axb5 9. Nxb5 $1 Qb6 10. Nd6+ Kf8 11. exf6 Bxf6 12. Nc4 Qd8 13.
d4 {[ Although the Rh8 is out of play the rest of Black's position is quite
good he will have two bishops, centre pawns, and queenside files. White must
play for the initiative. ]} cxd4 14. Bh6+ Kg8 (14... Bg7 15. Bxg7+ Kxg7 16.
Nxd4 $16) 15. Nce5 d6 16. Nxc6 bxc6 17. Nxd4 Bd7 18. c3 c5 19. Nf3 Bc6 20. Nh2
Ra7 21. Qd2 Bg7 22. Ng4 Bxh6 23. Qxh6 Qf8 24. Qf4 h5 25. Ne3 Qg7 26. Qc4 Qf6 {
[ Black is on the verge of extricating himself so White initiates some more
tactics ]} 27. b4 Ra3 28. b5 $1 Bb7 (28... Rxc3 29. Qa4 Bb7 30. Qa7 $18) 29.
Nd5 Qg5 {[ A very brave move missed by the commentary room, 29..Bxd5 30.Qxd5
Kg7 idea 31.b6 Rb8 was also playable ]} 30. Nxe7+ Kg7 31. Nc6 Bxc6 32. bxc6 Rc8
33. Qb5 Qd5 $2 {[ A shame, after great defence Black, in time pressure, misses
a cheapo. ]} (33... Ra7 $1 {[ /\ Rbc7 or Qd5 should be OK for Black ]}) 34. c4
$1 {[#] [ /\ Qb2+ +- ]} Qd4 35. Rad1 Qf6 36. Re2 $1 $16 (36. Rxd6 Qxd6 37. Qb2+
Qd4 38. Qxa3 Rxc6 {[ Is much better for Black than the game ]}) 36... Ra7 37.
Red2 Re7 38. Rxd6 Re1+ 39. Rxe1 Qxd6 40. a4 Rxc6 41. a5 Ra6 42. g3 Qd2 43. Ra1
Rf6 44. Qxc5 Qc3 45. Qa3 Qd4 46. Ra2 h4 47. g4 Qxc4 48. Qb2 Qd3 49. Ra1 Qxh3
50. Qd4 g5 51. a6 Kg6 52. a7 Rf4 53. Qxf4 $1 1-0

