1. e4 c6 2. d3 {[ A good choice since Julian plays the Caro as well and is
therefore less likely to take on the main lines ]} d5 3. Nd2 e5 4. Ngf3 Bd6 5.
g3 Nf6 6. Bg2 O-O 7. O-O Re8 8. h3 {[ This seems a bit ponderous, 8.Re1 seems
more to the point ]} Nbd7 9. Re1 Nf8 10. Nh4 Ng6 11. Nf5 Bxf5 $5 {[ 11..Bf8
was the 'normal' move, the commentary room thought White might start a
kingside pawn roller now. ]} 12. exf5 Nf8 13. Nf1 Qb6 14. Ne3 {[ 14.g4 h6 15.
Ng3 looks better then White can force through h4 and g5. Now Black prevents
this ]} Rad8 15. g4 h6 16. h4 N8h7 17. g5 $2 {[ This ruins White's position,
and should have lost him the game ]} hxg5 18. hxg5 Nxg5 19. Nxd5 Nxd5 20. Bxg5
Be7 {[ White is now going to be left with a very bad bishop ]} 21. Qg4 $5 {
[ The commentary room thought this was pure bluff, and so it was! ]} Bxg5 22.
Qxg5 Rd6 $1 $17 23. Re4 {[ This was really trying it on ]} Qd8 $2 {[ The bluff
works ! ]} (23... Qxb2 24. Rae1 (24. Rg4 Qxa1+ 25. Bf1 e4 $19) 24... Nf6 25.
Rh4 Nh7 26. Qh5 Rh6 $19 {[ Commentary room ]}) 24. Qxd8 Rdxd8 25. Rae1 {
[ Now White gets so much play he can overcome his structural weaknesses ]} f6
26. d4 Nf4 27. Bf1 Kf8 28. dxe5 Rxe5 29. Rxe5 fxe5 30. Rxe5 Rd4 31. f3 Kf7 32.
Kf2 Kf6 33. Ra5 Rd7 34. Rxa7 Kxf5 35. Ba6 Rd2+ 36. Ke3 Rxc2 37. Rxb7 g5 $2 (
37... c5 $1 {[ /\ Ng2+ Kd3 Ne1+ with a draw ]}) 38. a4 $2 (38. Bd3+ Nxd3 39.
Kxd3 $16) 38... Ke5 39. Bf1 $4 c5 $4 {[#]} (39... Nd5+ $1 40. Kd3 Rf2 $19 {
[ Mestel ]}) 40. Re7+ 1/2-1/2

