1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 c5 4. e3 Bg7 5. Nc3 O-O 6. Be2 d5 7. O-O Nc6 8. h3
cxd4 9. exd4 dxc4 10. Bxc4 Na5 11. Be2 Be6 12. Re1 Rc8 {[ Black is already at
least equal ]} 13. Bg5 h6 14. Bh4 Nd5 (14... Bc4 15. Rc1 Bxe2 16. Qxe2 Re8 $10)
(14... Nc4 15. Na4 Nd6 16. Nc5 Bd5 $15 {[ /\ Nf5 ]}) 15. Rc1 Nxc3 16. bxc3 Bf6
$2 {[ A complete misjudgement, Black was worried about the pressure on e7 but
this was no the way to relieve it. White now gets a passed d pawn and soon, a
clear advantage ]} (16... Re8 17. Bb5 Bd7 $10) (16... Nc4 $10) 17. Bxf6 exf6
18. Qa4 Bc4 19. Bxc4 Rxc4 20. Qa3 b6 21. Re7 $16 Rc7 22. Rxc7 Qxc7 23. c4 {
[ With hindsight it looks like Black's reply should have lost a piece but
maybe not in which case this may not be best ]} Nxc4 $5 {[#]} 24. Qb4 $1 {
[ Missed that (Hodgson) ! ]} (24. Qb3 Rc8 25. Nd2 Nxd2 26. Rxc7 Rxc7 {[
Threatens Rc1+ with a draw and gives Black drawing chances ]}) 24... Rc8 {
[ Black now stays in the game with some miraculous resources. After the game
the players thought Black should have lost a piece but I cannot see it ]} 25.
Nd2 b5 26. Qxb5 Qb6 27. Qa4 Qb2 $1 {[ Only move ]} 28. Qc2 (28. Rxc4 Rxc4 29.
Nxc4 Qc1+ 30. Kh2 Qf4+ 31. Kg1 Qc1+ $10) (28. Nb3 {[ This was thought after
the game to be decisive since it defends c1 ]} Qe2 (28... Nb6 29. Rxc8+ Nxc8
30. Qe8+ $18 {[ The knight guards c1 ]}) 29. d5 (29. Na5 Qd2 $1) (29. Qd7 Qe6))
(28. Rc2 Nb6) 28... Qxc2 29. Rxc2 Nb6 30. Rxc8+ Nxc8 31. Kf1 {[ This ending
looked very good for White but afterwards Mark felt that a c pawn instead of a
d pawn, one file further from the kingside may been winning. In the game the
Black knight manages to cover both sides ]} Kf8 32. Ke2 Ke7 33. Nc4 Kd7 34. Kd3
Kc6 35. Ne3 f5 36. f4 h5 37. h4 f6 38. Kc4 Nd6+ 39. Kb4 Ne4 40. a4 Ng3 41. Kc4
Ne2 42. Nd5 Kd6 43. a5 a6 44. Nb4 Nxf4 45. Nxa6 Nxg2 46. Nb4 Ne3+ 47. Kd3 f4 $1
{[ Now the very real possibility of 3 Black kingside passed pawns forced White
to bale out ]} 48. a6 Kc7 49. d5 Nf5 50. Ke4 f3 51. d6+ $1 $10 Nxd6+ 52. Kxf3
Nf5 53. Nd5+ Kb8 54. Nxf6 Nxh4+ 55. Kf4 Ka7 56. Nxh5 gxh5 57. Kg5 Ng6 58. Kxh5
Kxa6 59. Kxg6 {[#]} 1/2-1/2

