1. e4 h6 2. d4 c5 3. d5 d6 4. Nc3 g5 5. Be2 Nf6 6. Nf3 Nbd7 {[ The Basman
version of the Benoni, positionally well motivated by the strongpost on e5 but
on the downside, the kingside pawns are weakened ]} 7. a4 a6 8. h4 g4 9. Nd2
Ne5 $2 {[ After this Black seems to be positionally lost since White
systematically gangs up on the g pawn. 9..h5 was better but then White could
continue with Nf1-g3 and Bg5 with some advantage. ]} 10. h5 $1 {[#]} g3 {
[ One of Basman's pupils predicted this in the commentary room but it does not
help ]} 11. f3 Rg8 12. Nf1 Bd7 13. Bf4 Qb6 14. Qc1 e6 {[ Black attempts to
expose the White king ]} 15. Nxg3 O-O-O 16. Kf2 exd5 17. exd5 Re8 18. Qd2 {
[ Now White has a very strong plan of a5 Na4 and after the exchange of knight
for the Bd7 the f5 square drops off and with it the Black position ]} Bg7 19.
a5 Qc7 20. Na4 Bh8 21. Nb6+ Kb8 22. Rae1 c4 {[ Black's play becomes
increasingly desperate but he has no play at all ]} 23. Qb4 $1 Rxg3 {[ The
best chance to keep the game going ]} 24. Kxg3 (24. Bxg3 Neg4+ 25. fxg4 Ne4+
26. Kf3 Bxg4+ 27. Kxg4 Rg8+) 24... Bb5 25. Kf2 Neg4+ 26. fxg4 Ne4+ 27. Kf3 Bd4
28. Bxc4 Bc5 29. Qb3 f5 {[ Basman was in time pressure so he gives it one last
fling ]} 30. gxf5 Qg7 31. Bxb5 Rg8 32. g3 Nd2+ 33. Bxd2 Qxg3+ 34. Ke2 Qg2+ 35.
Kd1 axb5 1-0

