1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Nf3 Bb4 7. cxd5 exd5 8.
Ne5 O-O 9. Bd3 Ne4 10. O-O Bxc3 11. bxc3 Nd7 12. Qc2 Nxe5 13. dxe5 Bf5 14. Be3
Rc8 15. Bd4 Bg6 16. e6 $5 {[ Mark sacrifices for the initiative and to weaken
the Black pawns ]} fxe6 17. f3 Nxc3 $1 18. Bxg6 hxg6 19. Qb2 (19. Bxc3 d4 $17)
19... Na4 20. Qxb7 Rf7 21. Qa6 Nb6 22. Rae1 Rc6 (22... Qd6 $2 23. Bxb6 Qxb6+
24. Qxb6 axb6 25. Rxe6 $16) 23. Qd3 Qc8 $5 {[ Offering the pawn back to
produce a drawish position. Objectively White should gone for that because he
now takes a lot of risks and stands worse. ]} 24. Ba1 (24. Bxb6 axb6 25. Qxg6
Rf6 26. Qd3 Rc2 $10) 24... Nc4 25. Rf2 (25. Qxg6 e5 26. Qd3 d4 $17 {[
Commentary room ]}) 25... g5 $1 26. Rfe2 Qd7 27. h3 Rf8 28. Rd1 Qf7 29. Qd4
Rfc8 (29... Rd8 $1 {[ /\ e5 d4 ]} 30. Qg4 Qf4 $17) 30. Qf2 Nd6 31. Qe3 {
[ White wins back the pawn but now Black gets a very strong initiative ]} Nf5
32. Qxg5 Rc2 33. Rxc2 Rxc2 34. Be5 (34. g4 $2 Qc7 $19) 34... Re2 35. Bc3 Qc7 $1
(35... Ne3 $5) 36. Rc1 Qb6+ (36... Ne3 $2 37. Bd2 $1) 37. Kh2 Qe3 (37... Qf2
38. Bxg7 Nxg7 39. Rc8+ Kh7 40. Rc7 Qd4 41. Qh5+ Kg8 42. Rc8+) 38. Qxe3 Nxe3 39.
Re1 Rxe1 40. Bxe1 d4 41. Bf2 Nc2 42. Kg1 Kf7 43. Kf1 e5 44. Ke2 Ke6 45. h4 Nb4
(45... Kf5 {[ /\ a6 e4 ]} 46. g4+ Kf4 $1) 46. a3 Nd5 47. g3 Nc3+ 48. Kd3 Kd5
49. g4 {[ White's kingside pawns save the day ]} Nd1 50. Bg3 Nb2+ 51. Ke2 e4
52. fxe4+ Kxe4 53. Bb8 $1 $10 d3+ 54. Ke1 a5 55. h5 Nc4 56. g5 Kf5 57. h6 gxh6
58. gxh6 Kg6 59. a4 Kxh6 60. Bc7 Kg6 1/2-1/2

