1. d4 Nf6 2. Bg5 Ne4 3. h4 c5 4. d5 {[ According to Ali Mortazavi, another h4
practitioner, he and Julian had become tired of 4.dxc5 so this possibility was
briefly considered ]} g6 5. Qd3 Qa5+ 6. Nd2 Nxg5 7. hxg5 Bg7 8. c3 d6 9. e4 Nd7
10. a4 $14 {[ The white knight's strong post on c4 assures him of some
advantage ]} Rb8 11. Nc4 Qc7 12. f4 a6 (12... b6 13. Nf3 a6 14. Be2 b5 15. axb5
axb5 {[ Looks playable ]} 16. Ne3 c4 17. Qc2) 13. a5 b5 14. axb6 Nxb6 15. Qc2
e6 16. dxe6 Bxe6 17. Ne3 Bd7 18. Nf3 O-O 19. f5 Rfe8 20. f6 Bf8 21. O-O-O {
[ Now if Black does not react he will be mated very quickly ]} d5 22. e5 $2 (
22. Nxd5 Nxd5 23. Rxd5 Bc6 24. Bc4 $1 $16) 22... Rxe5 $1 $17 23. Qf2 Rxe3 24.
Qxe3 d4 $2 (24... Bd6 $1 $17) 25. Qe1 $13 dxc3 26. Qxc3 Qf4+ (26... Na4 27. Qe5
) 27. Rd2 Qa4 28. b3 $1 {[ The prelude to an incredible concept, the
commentary room thought White had to play 28.Qa3 ]} Qa3+ 29. Qb2 Qa5 {[#] [ A
remarkable position, White looks to be helpless against the threats of ..c4 ..
Ba3 etc but a brilliant combination from Julian exploits the imprisoned black
king. ]} 30. Rxd7 $1 c4 $5 {[ Brace yourselves ]} (30... Nxd7 $5 31. Bc4 {
[ At first I thought this was good for white but maybe not, Black's 30th,
while entertaining the crowd and giving the impression of winning on the spot,
may have been the decisive mistake. ]} Bd6 $1 $13 (31... Nb6 $2 32. Bxf7+ $1
Kxf7 33. Ne5+ Kg8 (33... Ke6 34. Nc6 $18) 34. f7+ $18)) 31. Rxf7 $3 {[#]} Ba3 (
31... Kxf7 32. Ne5+ $1 Ke6 (32... Kg8 33. f7+ $18) (32... Ke8 33. f7+ {[ /\
Nc6+ +- ]}) 33. Bxc4+ $1 $18) 32. Rg7+ $1 {[ Essential, so that Rhh7 threatens
mate ]} Kf8 33. Rhxh7 {[#] [ An incredible position. The queen is going with
check but the white king can escape the attentions of queen rook and knight
and make it to h2 g3, amazed ? you will be ]} Bxb2+ 34. Kd1 $4 {[ With 5
minutes on the clock to John's 1 Julian makes a losing blunder. It is
reasonable to assume that recapturing the bishop loses but in fact it wins. ]}
(34. Kxb2 Na4+ 35. Kc1 Qc3+ 36. Kd1 Nb2+ 37. Ke2 Qd3+ 38. Kf2 Nd1+ 39. Kg1 $1
Qe3+ 40. Kh2 $18) 34... Qd5+ $4 {[ Black lost on time but he is now lost. 35.
Nd2 forces 35..Qg8 going into a lost ending, a bizarre end to a very
entertaining game ]} (34... Bxf6 $3 35. gxf6 Qa1+ 36. Ke2 Qxf6 $19) 1-0

