1. d4 d6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 Nd7 5. e4 e5 6. Be2 Ne7 7. O-O O-O 8. Be3 (
8. Re1 f5 9. dxe5 dxe5 10. exf5 gxf5 11. Bg5 $14) 8... h6 {[ x g5, 8..c6!? ]}
9. Qd2 Kh7 10. Rad1 f5 11. dxe5 dxe5 12. exf5 gxf5 13. Qc2 $1 {[ An extremely
clever move, the Qd8 is now uncomfortably placed and the disruptive ..f4
prevented. Ideas of Nh4 and Bc5 convince Black of the need to unpin and
therefore to prevent Nd5 ]} c6 (13... Ng6 14. Bd3 $1 e4 15. Nxe4 fxe4 16. Bxe4
Qe8 17. Nh4 $18) 14. Rd6 Qc7 15. Rfd1 Ng6 $2 (15... Rf6 $8 16. c5 $16 {[ xd6
xe5 xf5 ]}) 16. Rxg6 $1 $16 {[#]} Kxg6 17. Nh4+ Kf7 18. Nxf5 Nf6 $8 19. Nd6+ $1
{[ The key is to keep the black queen out of f7 then Qg6 Bxh6 Rd3 follows ]}
Kg8 20. Qg6 Be6 21. Bxh6 Rad8 22. c5 Kh8 23. Bd3 Bg8 24. Qg5 Bh7 25. Bxg7+ Qxg7
26. Qxe5 $18 Bxd3 $2 {[ Time trouble ]} 27. Rxd3 Rde8 28. Nxe8 Rxe8 29. Qxe8+
$1 Nxe8 30. Rh3+ 1-0

