experiment to which White later attributed many of his coming woes. The knight
just seems to get in the way from now on ]} c6 8. O-O a6 9. b3 b5 10. cxb5 axb5
11. Bb2 Re8 12. Qc2 Bf8 13. Rfd1 b4 14. Nb1 $6 {[ 14.Na4 /\ Rac1 ]} Ba6 $1 $15
{[ xe2 d3 ]} 15. dxe5 dxe5 16. Nc1 Qb6 $17 {[ x f2, eventually White cannot
hold this square ]} 17. h3 Nc5 18. a3 Rad8 19. Rd2 bxa3 20. Bxa3 Ne6 21. Bxf8
Rxf8 22. Rxd8 Rxd8 23. Nc3 h5 $1 24. h4 $6 Ng4 $18 25. Qb2 Nd4 26. b4 Be2 $3 {
[#] [ 27.N1xe2 Nf3+ ! a, 28.Bxf3 Qxf2+ 29. Kh1 Qh2# b, 28.Kf1 Qxf2# c, 28.Kh1
Nxf2# ]} 0-1

