1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 b6 5. Nge2 Bb7 6. a3 Be7 7. d5 O-O 8. Ng3
d6 (8... Re8 $5 {[ /\ b5!? ]}) 9. e4 Nbd7 10. Be2 Re8 11. O-O a6 $6 (11... c6
$14) 12. Bf4 $1 {[ xd6 ]} Rc8 13. Qd2 Nf8 14. Rad1 Qd7 15. Be3 $1 $16 {[ x b6 ]
} Qd8 16. b4 c6 $2 17. e5 $1 $18 cxd5 (17... N6d7 18. exd6 Bxd6 19. dxc6 Rxc6
20. b5 $18) 18. exf6 Bxf6 19. Na4 dxc4 20. Nxb6 d5 {[ Best practical chance ]}
21. Nxc8 Qxc8 22. f4 Bd8 23. Qc3 Nd7 24. Bf3 Nb6 {[ The battle now revolves
around the d5 square which Black needs to protect in order to play e5 ]} 25.
Kh1 Na4 26. Qc2 Bc6 27. Ne2 Kh8 28. Bd4 f6 29. Ba1 Nb6 30. Nc3 Bc7 31. g3 Rd8
32. Qg2 Qa8 33. Rd2 e5 34. fxe5 fxe5 35. Nxd5 $1 {[#] [ Just when Black looks
like he is getting some chances this well calculated tactical blow finishes
the game ]} Rxd5 (35... Nxd5 36. Rfd1 Ne7 37. Rxd8+ Bxd8 38. Bxc6 Nxc6 39. Rd6
$18) 36. Rxd5 Nxd5 37. Rd1 Nxb4 (37... Ne3 38. Bxc6 $18) 38. Bxc6 Nxc6 39. Rd7
Qb7 40. h4 Qb6 41. Qf3 Qb1+ 42. Kh2 Qc2+ 43. Kh3 {[ Although Black has won
back some material he has no coordination and cannot defend his back rank so ]}
1-0

